2
00:00:13,803 --> 00:00:18,747
<font color="#4096d1">本字幕仅供学习交流，严禁用于商业用途

3
00:00:24,879 --> 00:00:31,970
<font color="#4096d1">-=破烂熊字幕组=- 翻译: tanya312 校对&时间轴: tpring

4
00:00:35,813 --> 00:00:38,929
利益冲突

5
00:00:43,759 --> 00:00:45,954
早上好 首相
Good morning, Prime Minister.

6
00:00:47,199 --> 00:00:49,793
早上好 首相
Good morning, Prime Minister.

7
00:00:49,959 --> 00:00:51,950
您在看报纸吗?
Is it the newspapers?

8
00:00:52,999 --> 00:00:57,539
是啊 家家都说自我上任以来
Yes. They all say that since my administration came into office

9
00:00:57,539 --> 00:00:58,710
一切都毫无变化
nothing has changed.

10
00:00:58,919 --> 00:01:01,114
您一定特别自豪吧
You must be very proud.

11
00:01:02,319 --> 00:01:04,628
这可不是夸我 伯纳
That's not meant as a compliment.

12
00:01:04,799 --> 00:01:08,047
伦敦总共十份晨报 我全看了一遍
I read all ten of this morning's London papers.

13
00:01:08,047 --> 00:01:10,431
其中九份对我没说半句好话
Not a good word about me in nine of them.

14
00:01:10,599 --> 00:01:11,731
只有第十份好些?
But the tenth is better?

15
00:01:11,731 --> 00:01:15,070
第十份更糟 压根没提我
Worse. It doesn't mention me at all.

16
00:01:15,239 --> 00:01:16,931
今天早晨他们攻击您什么?
What have they got against you this moring?

17
00:01:16,931 --> 00:01:19,517
全都一个口径
They all say the same thing.

18
00:01:19,679 --> 00:01:21,670
说我是个绣花枕头
That I'm a windbag.

19
00:01:21,839 --> 00:01:24,399
老天啊      就是
Good heavens!      Yeah.

20
00:01:24,559 --> 00:01:26,057
真奇怪 不是吗?
Extraordinary, isn't it?

21
00:01:26,057 --> 00:01:28,154
他们说我的执政全是假大空
They say that my administration's all rhetoric.

22
00:01:28,319 --> 00:01:30,710
我说得天花乱坠 可是一事无成
That I talk and talk, but nothing ever gets done.

23
00:01:30,719 --> 00:01:32,710
睁眼说瞎话嘛
It simply isn't true.

24
00:01:32,879 --> 00:01:34,874
各项改革都在酝酿中
There are reforms in the pipeline,

25
00:01:34,879 --> 00:01:36,474
总方针已经今非昔比
a great change of direction.

26
00:01:36,639 --> 00:01:38,400
确立了新的发展观
New schemes of development,

27
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,473
执政理念不断升华
a whole new philosophy of government.

28
00:01:40,639 --> 00:01:43,000
社会结构取得长足进步
Profound change in the social fabric

29
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,076
国家地缘政治面貌也为之一新
and geopolitical climate of this country.

30
00:01:45,999 --> 00:01:48,593
那究竟有什么成就?
So what is actually happening?

31
00:01:49,519 --> 00:01:52,829
眼下还没有嘛
Nothing yet, obviously.

32
00:01:52,999 --> 00:01:56,435
准是汉弗莱爵士      请他进来吧
That'll be Sir Humphrey.      Better send him in.

33
00:01:56,599 --> 00:01:58,590
请汉弗莱爵士进来
Send Sir Humphrey in.

34
00:01:58,759 --> 00:02:01,472
这些批评大概都源自传闻中的
The origin of this criticism is this rumour

35
00:02:01,472 --> 00:02:02,752
金融城(伦敦内城)的丑闻
about a scandal in the City.

36
00:02:02,919 --> 00:02:05,638
你怎么知道?      首相
How did you guess?     Prime Minister.

37
00:02:05,799 --> 00:02:08,525
汉弗莱 我决定回应所有这些
Humphrey, I've decided to respond

38
00:02:08,525 --> 00:02:10,793
对金融城丑闻的批评
to all this criticism about a scandal in the City.

39
00:02:10,959 --> 00:02:13,268
媒体呼吁采取行动
The press is demanding action.

40
00:02:13,439 --> 00:02:15,069
您打算怎么办?
What are you proposing to do?

41
00:02:15,439 --> 00:02:18,069
我要...任命一个人
I shall... appoint... someone.

42
00:02:18,239 --> 00:02:20,952
您什么时候决定的?
When did you take this decision?

43
00:02:20,952 --> 00:02:21,834
今天 看报纸的时候
Today when I read the papers.

44
00:02:21,999 --> 00:02:25,150
您什么时候想到的呢?      今天 看报纸的时候
But when did you first think of it?      Today.

45
00:02:25,319 --> 00:02:28,274
那您花了多久权衡
And for how long did you weigh

46
00:02:28,274 --> 00:02:29,835
这决策的利弊呢?
the pros and cons of this decision?

47
00:02:29,999 --> 00:02:32,388
没多久 我决定要...拿出决心来
Not long. I decided to be decisive.

48
00:02:32,559 --> 00:02:34,914
首相 恕我直言 您未免太在乎
I think you worry too much

49
00:02:34,914 --> 00:02:35,756
那些报纸的说辞了
about what the papers say.

50
00:02:35,919 --> 00:02:38,638
只有公务员才能说得这么轻巧
Only a civil servant could make that remark.

51
00:02:38,799 --> 00:02:40,000
我不能不在乎
I have to worry about them,

52
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,508
政党大会就快召开了
with the party conference coming up.

53
00:02:42,679 --> 00:02:44,866
这流言怎么也平息不了
These rumours of a scandal won't go away.

54
00:02:44,866 --> 00:02:47,673
等它不只是流言再来操心吧
Let's not worry until it's more than a rumour.

55
00:02:47,839 --> 00:02:49,713
请您过目内阁议程
Here's the Cabinet agenda.

56
00:02:49,713 --> 00:02:51,388
先放着 汉弗莱 这件事严重多了
Not now. This is more important.

57
00:02:51,559 --> 00:02:56,002
恕难苟同 首相 关于媒体必须牢记的是
With respect, it is not. Remember, the press

58
00:02:56,002 --> 00:02:57,873
他们只迎合读者的偏见
just pander to their readers' prejudices.

59
00:02:58,039 --> 00:03:00,000
媒体的事我不用你教
Don't tell me about the press.

60
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,236
报纸读者我最熟悉了
I know exactly who reads the papers.

61
00:03:01,399 --> 00:03:02,500
"镜报"的读者是
The "Mirror" is read by people

62
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,596
自以为在治理国家的人
who think they run the country.

63
00:03:04,759 --> 00:03:06,000
"卫报"的读者是
The "Guardian" is read by people

64
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,468
自以为应该治理国家的人
who think they OUGHT to run it.

65
00:03:08,639 --> 00:03:10,000
"泰晤士报"的读者是
The "Times" is read by the people

66
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,029
真的在治理国家的人
who DO run the country.

67
00:03:12,199 --> 00:03:13,529
"每日邮报"的读者是
The "Daily Mail" is read by the wives

68
00:03:13,529 --> 00:03:15,874
治理国家的人的夫人
of the people who run it.

69
00:03:16,039 --> 00:03:18,032
"金融时报"的读者是
The "Financial Times" is read by people

70
00:03:18,039 --> 00:03:20,032
手里攥着国家的人
who OWN the country.

71
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:22,865
"晨星报"的读者是想把国家
The "Morning Star" is read by people who think

72
00:03:22,865 --> 00:03:25,432
交给别国治理的人
the country should be run by another country

73
00:03:25,599 --> 00:03:27,155
而"每日电讯报"的读者
and the "Daily Telegraph"

74
00:03:27,155 --> 00:03:29,387
觉得我们正被别国治理着
is read by people who think it is.

75
00:03:32,359 --> 00:03:35,157
首相 那"太阳报"的读者呢?
What about the people who read "The Sun"?

76
00:03:35,319 --> 00:03:37,208
"太阳报"的读者不在乎谁治理国家
"Sun" readers don't care who runs the country

77
00:03:37,208 --> 00:03:40,074
只要她前凸后翘就行
as long as she's got big tits.

78
00:03:49,559 --> 00:03:50,993
你怎么看
What do you make of

79
00:03:50,993 --> 00:03:53,199
菲利普-贝伦森银行的事 戴斯蒙?
this Phillips Berenson business, Desmond?

80
00:03:53,199 --> 00:03:56,191
恐怕不妙      比媒体说的还糟?
Not too good.      Worse than the press are saying?

81
00:03:56,359 --> 00:03:58,318
不止是一家投资银行
More than another investment bank

82
00:03:58,319 --> 00:04:00,318
投错了资的问题?
that made the wrong investments?

83
00:04:00,479 --> 00:04:02,947
恐怕是 这才冰山一角呢
'Fraid so. Tip of the iceberg.

84
00:04:03,119 --> 00:04:05,838
具体说说      他们坏了规矩
Tell me more.       They've broken the rules.

85
00:04:05,999 --> 00:04:07,990
内线交易潜规则吗?
The insider trading regulations?

86
00:04:08,159 --> 00:04:10,548
不是      那就好
No.      That's one relief.

87
00:04:10,719 --> 00:04:11,894
这条当然首当其冲 可他们
Of course they've broken those,

88
00:04:11,894 --> 00:04:15,031
还坏了金融城的基本规矩
but they've broken the basic rule of the City.

89
00:04:15,199 --> 00:04:19,397
我都不知道他们还有规矩      就一条
I didn't know there were any.      Just the one.

90
00:04:19,559 --> 00:04:21,454
你要是能力差 就得诚实
If you're incompetent, you have to be honest.

91
00:04:21,454 --> 00:04:23,806
你要想耍花招 就得聪明
If you're crooked, you have to be clever.

92
00:04:24,719 --> 00:04:27,666
如果你诚实 搞出了岔子
If you're honest and make a pig's breakfast of things

93
00:04:27,666 --> 00:04:28,917
大家会拉你一把
chaps help you out.

94
00:04:29,079 --> 00:04:30,720
耍花招呢?
If you're crooked?

95
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:33,072
有利可图的话 谁也不过问
With good profits, chaps don't ask questions.

96
00:04:33,239 --> 00:04:35,958
他们又不蠢 至少没那么蠢
They're not stupid. Well, not that stupid.

97
00:04:36,119 --> 00:04:38,872
所以理想的公司得既诚实又聪明?
The ideal is a firm which is honest and clever?

98
00:04:39,039 --> 00:04:41,000
对 万一你碰上了
Yes. Let me know if you ever

99
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,157
可要告诉我啊
come across one, won't you?

100
00:04:43,319 --> 00:04:46,311
贝伦森银行呢?      他们嘛...
And Phillips Berenson?      Well, they were...

101
00:04:46,479 --> 00:04:49,676
犯法了      话不能这么说
Breaking the law.      I wouldn't put it like that.

102
00:04:49,839 --> 00:04:53,042
银行董事不是把资本
Were the directors siphoning off funds

103
00:04:53,042 --> 00:04:53,832
抽到自己公司去了吗?
into their own companies?

104
00:04:53,999 --> 00:04:55,808
可能会还回来呢
Might've paid it back later.

105
00:04:55,808 --> 00:04:56,388
不过没还
But didn't.

106
00:04:56,559 --> 00:04:57,631
是暂时没还
Well, they haven't yet.

107
00:04:59,068 --> 00:05:00,678
逃税
Tax fiddles.

108
00:05:00,678 --> 00:05:02,109
他们自有一套办法
They placed their own interpretation

109
00:05:02,119 --> 00:05:04,109
解释财政部规章
on Treasury regulations.

110
00:05:04,279 --> 00:05:06,795
总得有人解释吧
Someone has to interpret them.

111
00:05:06,795 --> 00:05:08,795
财政部出台的解释呢?
What about the Treasury's interpretation?

112
00:05:09,839 --> 00:05:11,830
似乎不大好用吧
It didn't seem appropriate.

113
00:05:12,959 --> 00:05:15,857
资本转移到中欧小国公司去了?
Capital transfers to Liechtenstein companies?

114
00:05:15,857 --> 00:05:16,602
有这么回事
Bit of that.

115
00:05:16,602 --> 00:05:17,471
行贿呢?
Bribery?

116
00:05:17,471 --> 00:05:20,905
外国政府官员私下吃了回扣
Undisclosed commissions to foreign officials.

117
00:05:20,905 --> 00:05:22,709
就是行贿      对
Bribery.      Yes.

118
00:05:24,399 --> 00:05:26,390
您的白兰地      谢谢
Your brandies.      Thank you.

119
00:05:26,559 --> 00:05:28,948
可以买单了吗?      就来 先生
May I have the bill?      Certainly, sir.

120
00:05:30,239 --> 00:05:32,405
那整个内幕什么时候会泄露?
So when's all this going to come out?

121
00:05:32,405 --> 00:05:34,027
问题就在这 不能泄露
That's just it, it mustn't.

122
00:05:34,199 --> 00:05:35,908
你有什么办法?
How do you stop it?

123
00:05:35,909 --> 00:05:38,359
不知道 这就是我说的坏了规矩了
That's what I meant about breaking the rules.

124
00:05:38,359 --> 00:05:39,705
如果利润够高
If they were profitable,

125
00:05:39,705 --> 00:05:41,071
什么也不必泄露
it wouldn't need to come out.

126
00:05:41,239 --> 00:05:43,630
现在他们要破产了 真急人
Now they're going bust, I'm worried.

127
00:05:43,639 --> 00:05:45,630
你有牵涉吗?
Are you involved?

128
00:05:46,919 --> 00:05:49,877
像你们这么大的银行肯定没事吧?
Surely a huge bank like yours isn't affected?

129
00:05:50,039 --> 00:05:53,954
借你吉言 不过我们投了不少 有4亿呢
I wish you were right, but we've supported

130
00:05:55,119 --> 00:05:57,112
你说起来轻巧 汉弗莱
It's all very well for you,

131
00:05:57,119 --> 00:05:59,112
可是当你朝阿拉伯人...
but when you've got all that Arab mon...

132
00:05:59,279 --> 00:06:02,825
当你朝阿拉伯人贷了利率11%的款
When you've got all that Arab money at 11%,

133
00:06:02,825 --> 00:06:03,683
你若不想丢人现眼
you'd look pretty silly

134
00:06:03,683 --> 00:06:06,432
当然要以14%利率栽给别人
if you didn't lend it to somebody for 14.

135
00:06:08,679 --> 00:06:11,115
没几个人能稳出14%
You couldn't trust many people to pay 14.

136
00:06:11,115 --> 00:06:12,115
那当然
Obviously.

137
00:06:12,279 --> 00:06:14,747
于是我们继续追加 让它流动起来
Then we put in more to keep them afloat.

138
00:06:14,919 --> 00:06:16,308
要是你知道他们是骗子...
If you knew they were crooks...

139
00:06:16,308 --> 00:06:17,308
我们不知道
We didn't.

140
00:06:17,479 --> 00:06:19,870
你们可以调查啊
You could've made inquiries.

141
00:06:19,879 --> 00:06:21,870
金融城里没人调查这种事
You don't make such inquiries in the City.

142
00:06:22,039 --> 00:06:24,234
他们看上去挺正派的
They seemed like decent chaps.

143
00:06:25,239 --> 00:06:27,949
正派人不该摸其他正派人的底
Decent chaps don't check up on decent chaps

144
00:06:27,949 --> 00:06:29,949
检查他们究竟正不正派
to see if they're behaving like decent chaps.

145
00:06:30,119 --> 00:06:33,395
糊涂大意值得交4亿学费吗?
And ignorance is worth paying 400 million for?

146
00:06:33,559 --> 00:06:36,156
糊涂是安全保障 上当受骗又不是犯罪
Ignorance is safety. It's not a crime to be deceived

147
00:06:36,159 --> 00:06:39,156
再说也不是我们自己的钱
And it's not our own money.

148
00:06:39,319 --> 00:06:41,071
您的账单 先生      谢谢
Your bill, sir.      Thank you.

149
00:06:41,239 --> 00:06:43,355
那接下来会怎样?
So what's going to happen?

150
00:06:43,519 --> 00:06:46,385
只有一个办法 由英格兰中央银行
Only one answer. The Bank of England

151
00:06:46,385 --> 00:06:47,512
出钱为贝伦森救市
must bail out Phillips Berenson.

152
00:06:47,679 --> 00:06:50,901
不声张 内部解决 大家就都能保本了
No publicity. That way we get our money back.

153
00:06:50,901 --> 00:06:52,116
纳税人买单
At the taxpayers' expense.

154
00:06:52,279 --> 00:06:54,270
当然      能办到吗?
Of course.      Can it be done?

155
00:06:54,439 --> 00:06:56,671
得看中央银行新董事长的意思
Depends on the new Bank of England Governor.

156
00:06:56,671 --> 00:06:58,671
还没任命呢
Hasn't been appointed yet.

157
00:06:58,839 --> 00:07:00,797
是啊 这就是我想谈的问题
That's what I wanted to talk about.

158
00:07:00,797 --> 00:07:01,797
会任命谁?
Who will it be?

159
00:07:01,959 --> 00:07:05,272
暂时没确定 不过据我所知首相
It isn't decided, but I understand from the PM

160
00:07:05,272 --> 00:07:07,272
最中意亚历山大-詹森
that the frontrunner is Alexander Jameson.

161
00:07:08,119 --> 00:07:10,713
不会吧 开什么玩笑      不开玩笑
You're joking? But that's impossible.

162
00:07:11,679 --> 00:07:14,070
你是说他太诚实了
You mean he's too honest.

163
00:07:14,079 --> 00:07:16,070
他还不止是自己诚实
It's not just that he behaves honestly.

164
00:07:17,639 --> 00:07:19,632
那倒没关系
That doesn't matter.

165
00:07:19,639 --> 00:07:21,632
我还有几个朋友也诚实
Some of my best friends behave honestly.

166
00:07:22,679 --> 00:07:25,671
没有耍花招的脑筋嘛
None are smart enough to get away with it.

167
00:07:25,839 --> 00:07:27,833
可詹森也不许别人不诚实
Jameson actually tries to stop dishonesty.

168
00:07:27,839 --> 00:07:30,833
那就完了 事不是这么办的
Fatal. The world doesn't work like that.

169
00:07:30,999 --> 00:07:33,544
是啊 他还写了份可怕的报告
Yes, he did that appalling report

170
00:07:33,544 --> 00:07:35,993
抨击公务员系统浪费资源 效率底下
on waste and inefficiency in the Civil Service.

171
00:07:37,079 --> 00:07:38,434
你得想办法拿掉他
You've got to block him.

172
00:07:38,434 --> 00:07:41,470
不好办 他是财政部推荐的
It's difficult. It's a Treasury recommendation.

173
00:07:41,639 --> 00:07:43,948
可最终得首相任命      对
But the PM makes the appointment.      Yes.

174
00:07:44,119 --> 00:07:46,838
还不止是贝伦森银行的问题
It's not just Phillips Berenson.

175
00:07:46,999 --> 00:07:48,992
一旦詹森开始顺藤摸瓜
Once Jameson starts his detective work,

176
00:07:48,999 --> 00:07:50,992
别的问题也会暴露出来
other things will come out.

177
00:07:51,159 --> 00:07:53,595
金融地震 信用崩溃 货币危机
Collapse of confidence,

178
00:07:53,595 --> 00:07:54,595
英镑会一落千丈
the pound will go through the floor.

179
00:07:54,759 --> 00:07:55,956
对 我明白
Yes, I see.

180
00:07:55,959 --> 00:07:57,956
你得让首相也明白
You must make the PM see it.

181
00:07:58,119 --> 00:08:00,833
信用可不能有闪失 金融城
Confidence mustn't be eroded. The City

182
00:08:00,833 --> 00:08:03,512
每年给国家进帐60亿
earns the country six billion pounds a year.

183
00:08:03,679 --> 00:08:05,834
总不能赌上这些 去追查几个家伙
You can't hazard that just because a few chaps

184
00:08:05,834 --> 00:08:08,445
瞒着股民 私下给朋友帮忙的事吧
do a few favours for friends.

185
00:08:08,445 --> 00:08:09,834
没道理嘛
Wouldn't be right.

186
00:08:14,079 --> 00:08:15,797
嗯...
Well...

187
00:08:18,119 --> 00:08:20,282
多萝西 我很不满意这份
Oh, Dorothy, I'm not happy about

188
00:08:20,282 --> 00:08:23,557
党派大会讲稿 里面没有好消息
my speech for the conference. It contains no good news.

189
00:08:23,719 --> 00:08:25,795
我们想不出好消息
We couldn't think of any.

190
00:08:26,803 --> 00:08:28,349
那就把坏消息往好了说
We'll have to make the bad news look good.

191
00:08:28,519 --> 00:08:30,908
我要讲讲医疗系统
I'll talk about the Health Service.

192
00:08:31,079 --> 00:08:33,436
关爱老人 关爱母婴
Care for the elderly, mothers and children,

193
00:08:33,436 --> 00:08:35,436
向健壮的国家迈进
growing up into a healthy nation.

194
00:08:35,599 --> 00:08:37,794
价廉物美?
Value for money?

195
00:08:37,959 --> 00:08:40,749
这个不能提 人人都知道
I can't say that. Everybody knows

196
00:08:40,959 --> 00:08:42,749
成本已经高得离谱了
that costs are completely out of control.

197
00:08:42,919 --> 00:08:44,910
是哦
Right.

198
00:08:45,079 --> 00:08:48,362
"我们正以前无古人的投资"
We are spending more than ever to make

199
00:08:48,362 --> 00:08:51,518
"打造世界一流的医疗系统"
our health service the best in the world.

200
00:08:51,679 --> 00:08:54,989
很好 再说国防
Good. Now, defence.

201
00:08:55,159 --> 00:08:58,153
我原本想谈削减军费的
I'd hoped to say something about defence cuts,

202
00:08:58,159 --> 00:09:00,153
可我还没说服他们削下一分钱
but I haven't persuaded them to make any yet.

203
00:09:00,319 --> 00:09:03,753
"本届政府不会将国家安全"
This government will not put the security

204
00:09:03,753 --> 00:09:04,312
"置之不顾"
of the nation in jeopardy

205
00:09:04,479 --> 00:09:07,471
"而去追求盲目虚假的节约"
by penny-pinching and... false economies?

206
00:09:07,639 --> 00:09:10,200
就算为了国家安全
Not that we'd put security in jeopardy

207
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:11,951
也只需要一所音乐学校
by having ONE service music school

208
00:09:12,119 --> 00:09:13,714
而不至于要三所
instead of three separate ones

209
00:09:13,719 --> 00:09:15,714
海陆空三军各一所吧
for the Army, Navy and RAF.

210
00:09:15,879 --> 00:09:17,873
总不至于海军吹起低音管来
There can hardly be a specifically

211
00:09:17,879 --> 00:09:20,873
也和其他人不同吧
Royal Naval method of playing bassoon.

212
00:09:21,039 --> 00:09:23,678
你不会把这写进去吧? 不 抱歉
You won't put that in? No, sorry.

213
00:09:24,599 --> 00:09:26,785
经济方面有利好消息吗?
Anything good we can say about the economy?

214
00:09:26,785 --> 00:09:29,627
经济是个问题 一点利好都没有
That's a problem. No good news at all.

215
00:09:29,799 --> 00:09:31,043
会找出些来的
We'll find something.

216
00:09:31,043 --> 00:09:34,748
会议期间不会爆出什么坏消息吧?
No bad news will break during the conference?

217
00:09:34,919 --> 00:09:37,993
问我干嘛 我只是个政治顾问
Don't ask me! I'm only the political adviser.

218
00:09:37,993 --> 00:09:39,993
您才有权看财政部秘密报告
YOU see the secret Treasury papers.

219
00:09:40,159 --> 00:09:42,949
我在琢磨贝伦森的丑闻
I was thinking about this Phillips Berenson

220
00:09:42,949 --> 00:09:44,949
你作何感想?
scandal. What do you make of it?

221
00:09:45,119 --> 00:09:47,314
大有蹊跷     怎么?
I'm suspicious.       Why?

222
00:09:47,479 --> 00:09:51,238
因为证券交易所主席 劳埃德银行主席
Because of the statements of the chairman

223
00:09:51,238 --> 00:09:52,348
和中央银行的声明
of the Stock Exchange and chairman of Lloyds.

224
00:09:52,519 --> 00:09:53,670
他们没发表声明
There were no statements.

225
00:09:53,670 --> 00:09:55,670
所以才蹊跷嘛
That's why I'm suspicious.

226
00:09:55,839 --> 00:09:57,770
如果传闻只是空穴来风
If there was nothing in these rumours,

227
00:09:57,770 --> 00:10:00,037
他们肯定争着出来撇清
they'd fall over themselves to say so.

228
00:10:00,199 --> 00:10:02,420
真不公平 金融城的丑闻总是
So unfair. Scandals in the City always look bad

229
00:10:02,420 --> 00:10:06,195
给政府抹黑 这跟我有什么关系
for the government. It's nothing to do with me.

230
00:10:06,359 --> 00:10:08,432
有了 我可以宣布
I know! I could announce

231
00:10:08,432 --> 00:10:10,432
为中央银行任命新董事长
the new Governor of the Bank of England.

232
00:10:10,599 --> 00:10:13,149
伯纳 去看看汉弗莱在不在
Bernard, see if you can see Humphrey around.

233
00:10:13,149 --> 00:10:15,992
跟他说我找他 说到哪了?
Tell him I'd like to see him. Where were we?

234
00:10:16,159 --> 00:10:18,151
经济 就业率有起色吗?
The economy. Unemployment coming down?

235
00:10:18,159 --> 00:10:19,151
没有
No.

236
00:10:19,319 --> 00:10:21,107
"我们将把减少失业"
We shall make the attack on unemployment

237
00:10:21,319 --> 00:10:23,107
"当作头等大事来抓" 薪水呢?
our top priority. Pay?

238
00:10:23,279 --> 00:10:25,114
涨得太快了
Rising too fast.

239
00:10:25,279 --> 00:10:28,114
"我们不能再透支了"
We cannot pay ourselves more than we earn.

240
00:10:28,279 --> 00:10:30,318
"世界其它国家没有义务赡养我们"
The world does not owe us a living.

241
00:10:30,319 --> 00:10:32,318
利息率呢?
Interest rates?

242
00:10:32,479 --> 00:10:35,722
太高了      大会前能降息?
Too high.      They might come down?

243
00:10:35,722 --> 00:10:37,028
那就太理想了
That'd be terrific.

244
00:10:37,028 --> 00:10:38,077
我没有那种好运气
I don't have that kind of luck.

245
00:10:38,239 --> 00:10:40,498
如果整个大局都惨不忍睹
If the whole picture's a total disaster,

246
00:10:40,498 --> 00:10:43,711
我们总还可以扯出国旗来吧
we can always wave the Union Jack.

247
00:10:43,879 --> 00:10:45,952
国家民族的伟大使命...
The nation's great destiny...

248
00:10:45,952 --> 00:10:47,952
在世界舞台上的独特位置
Unique role on the world stage.

249
00:10:48,119 --> 00:10:51,281
尽一切可能 建设一个繁荣昌盛的未来
Make every effort to build a prosperous world

250
00:10:51,281 --> 00:10:53,068
造福下一代 下下一代
for our children and our children's children.

251
00:10:53,239 --> 00:10:56,629
大概也只有他们能看到了
That's probably about how long it'll take.

252
00:10:57,797 --> 00:10:59,077
进来
YES?

253
00:10:59,079 --> 00:11:00,987
汉弗莱爵士 首相问您
The PM wonders

254
00:11:00,987 --> 00:11:02,071
能不能在五分钟之内过去
if you could join him in five minutes.

255
00:11:02,239 --> 00:11:04,628
没问题 伯纳 伯纳...
Certainly, Bernard. Bernard...

256
00:11:04,799 --> 00:11:06,587
中央银行的董事任命
Any news about the governorship

257
00:11:06,587 --> 00:11:08,587
有什么新消息吗?
of the Bank of England?

258
00:11:08,759 --> 00:11:10,788
首相正计划
The Prime Minister is planning

259
00:11:10,788 --> 00:11:13,549
任命亚历山大-詹森 清廉先生
to appoint Alexander Jameson. Mr Clean.

260
00:11:13,719 --> 00:11:15,518
这倒是个喜讯
That's one bit of good news.

261
00:11:15,518 --> 00:11:16,597
这是噩耗
Appalling news!

262
00:11:18,159 --> 00:11:20,231
您会劝首相改变主意吗?
Will you try and change the PM's mind?

263
00:11:20,231 --> 00:11:21,231
不
No.

264
00:11:21,399 --> 00:11:23,754
我会改变首相的主意
I WILL change the PM's mind.

265
00:11:23,919 --> 00:11:25,912
他似乎对詹森很有信心
He seems very keen on him.

266
00:11:25,919 --> 00:11:27,912
我知道 这就是我的出发点
That'll be my starting point.

267
00:11:28,079 --> 00:11:29,721
如果你想暗示
When you wish to suggest

268
00:11:29,721 --> 00:11:32,152
某个人不适合某个位置...
that somebody is not the ideal choice...

269
00:11:32,319 --> 00:11:34,870
就要诋毁他?
You rubbish them?

270
00:11:34,870 --> 00:11:36,870
第一步是要表示完全的支持
The first stage is to express absolute support.

271
00:11:37,039 --> 00:11:38,236
为什么
Why?

272
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:40,236
你不想留下说人坏话的记录吧
You don't want to say somebody's no good.

273
00:11:40,399 --> 00:11:42,594
你得显得像他的朋友
You must be seen to be their friend.

274
00:11:42,759 --> 00:11:45,436
说到底 先得绕到人后面
After all, it is necessary to get behind someone

275
00:11:45,759 --> 00:11:48,436
才能从背后捅刀子
before you can stab them in the back.

276
00:11:49,439 --> 00:11:51,969
可詹森是个好人
But Alexander Jameson is good.

277
00:11:51,969 --> 00:11:53,397
他极其诚实 又有能力
He's honest and efficient.

278
00:11:53,397 --> 00:11:55,867
太好了 这就进入第二步
Excellent. That's the second stage.

279
00:11:56,039 --> 00:11:57,430
你列举他所有的优点
You list his praiseworthy qualities,

280
00:11:57,439 --> 00:12:00,430
尤其是那些让他不称职的
especially those that make him unsuitable.

281
00:12:00,599 --> 00:12:02,467
大肆夸奖它们
You praise them to the point

282
00:12:02,467 --> 00:12:04,797
到矫枉过正的地步 这是第三步
where they become a vice. The third stage.

283
00:12:04,959 --> 00:12:08,431
更好的办法是 你把他的观点扁平化
Or, better still, you over-simplify his views

284
00:12:08,431 --> 00:12:10,431
给它们贴标签 就像你刚说的
by labelling them, as you just did.

285
00:12:10,599 --> 00:12:13,796
清廉先生?      对
You mean Mr Clean?       Yes.

286
00:12:13,959 --> 00:12:16,749
不过我想我们能做得更好
But I think we can do better than that.

287
00:12:16,959 --> 00:12:18,749
坐下吧 伯纳
Do sit down, Bernard.

288
00:12:18,919 --> 00:12:20,913
他不是常去教堂吗?
Isn't he a churchgoer?

289
00:12:20,913 --> 00:12:23,691
对 我记得他做过业余传道士
Yes, I believe he was once a lay preacher.

290
00:12:23,691 --> 00:12:24,150
很久以前了
A long time ago.

291
00:12:24,150 --> 00:12:26,669
太妙了 我们就用这点打击他
Splendid. We can use that against him.

292
00:12:26,839 --> 00:12:27,833
怎么做?
How?

293
00:12:27,839 --> 00:12:31,833
"多好的人啊 有生以来就没树过敌"
Charming man, hasn't an enemy in the world.

294
00:12:31,999 --> 00:12:34,197
"可他真能应付"
But is he really up to dealing with

295
00:12:34,199 --> 00:12:36,197
"金融城里那些恶棍吗?"
some of those rogues in the City?

296
00:12:36,359 --> 00:12:38,068
詹森很强硬的
Jameson's pretty tough.

297
00:12:38,069 --> 00:12:40,068
那就说他强硬过头了
Then we'll say he's too tough.

298
00:12:40,239 --> 00:12:43,029
这是第四步 列出他所有的缺陷
The fourth stage. You name all his bad points

299
00:12:43,239 --> 00:12:45,029
但要以为他开脱的口气
by defending and excusing them.

300
00:12:45,199 --> 00:12:47,590
就像 "哦 有什么关系"
You know - "Oh, it probably doesn't matter

301
00:12:47,590 --> 00:12:49,590
"不就是拒服兵役嘛"
that he was a conscientious objector.

302
00:12:49,759 --> 00:12:54,150
"我肯定...没人当真质疑他不爱国"
"I'm sure... nobody's really questioned his patriotism."

303
00:12:54,319 --> 00:12:57,273
或者 "我觉得大家批评他"
Or "I think the criticisms of him

304
00:12:57,273 --> 00:12:59,029
"搞垮了他上一家公司的事"
for bankrupting his last company

305
00:12:59,199 --> 00:13:01,713
"并不完全公平"
weren't entirely fair."

306
00:13:01,879 --> 00:13:03,603
这么说肯定奏效
That would certainly do it.

307
00:13:03,603 --> 00:13:07,078
如果不奏效 总还可以暗示有别的丑闻
If not, you can always hint at a hidden scandal.

308
00:13:07,239 --> 00:13:10,037
如果他单身 暗示他是同性恋
If he's not married, hint at homosexuality.

309
00:13:11,159 --> 00:13:13,957
如果结婚了呢?      那就通奸
If he is married?      Adultery.

310
00:13:14,119 --> 00:13:16,317
跟一位必须避讳的女士
With a lady's who's beyond reproach.

311
00:13:16,319 --> 00:13:18,317
比如皇室成员之类
One of the royals, for instance.

312
00:13:19,679 --> 00:13:21,829
或者电视女主播
Or a television newsreader.

313
00:13:23,519 --> 00:13:25,908
如果他显然婚姻幸福呢?
What if he's obviously happily married?

314
00:13:26,079 --> 00:13:29,073
说他是个道学先生 或者酗酒
Say he's extremely puritanical or he drinks

315
00:13:29,079 --> 00:13:31,073
或者在接受心理治疗 伯纳你看
or he's having psychiatric treatment.

316
00:13:31,239 --> 00:13:34,390
运用之妙 存乎一心啊 好好学着
The possibilities are endless. Listen and learn.

317
00:13:34,559 --> 00:13:36,550
对...
Yeah...

318
00:13:36,719 --> 00:13:38,710
汉弗莱爵士
Er, Sir Humphrey...

319
00:13:41,519 --> 00:13:42,512
首相
Prime Minister.

320
00:13:42,519 --> 00:13:45,512
汉弗莱 我们在准备我的党派大会讲话
We've been working on my conference speech.

321
00:13:45,679 --> 00:13:47,877
我很担心金融城丑闻的事
I'm worried about this scandal in the City.

322
00:13:47,879 --> 00:13:49,877
我看没那么严重吧 首相
I don't think it's very serious.

323
00:13:50,039 --> 00:13:51,480
当然严重
It certainly is.

324
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:53,236
不不 亲爱的女士
No, no, no, dear lady.

325
00:13:54,119 --> 00:13:57,111
银行朝一个大客户贷款过度 仅此而已
The bank over-lent to one big borrower, that's all.

326
00:13:57,279 --> 00:14:00,415
有些董事的过去不太干净
Some of its directors have a shady past.

327
00:14:00,415 --> 00:14:00,954
我看没这么简单
There's more to it.

328
00:14:01,119 --> 00:14:03,713
你能证明吗?      不能 是我的直觉
Can you prove it?       No, it's my antennae.

329
00:14:06,039 --> 00:14:08,170
明白了 首相 如今我们
I think, Prime Minister, that we are

330
00:14:08,170 --> 00:14:10,749
已经开始诉诸女性直觉了
in the realm of female intuition.

331
00:14:14,359 --> 00:14:16,827
走着瞧      那就走着瞧
We'll see.      We shall indeed.

332
00:14:18,199 --> 00:14:21,592
至少还有个喜讯 我决定任命
Anyway, the good news is I've decided to appoint

333
00:14:21,592 --> 00:14:23,592
詹森为中央银行董事长
Jameson as Governor of the Bank of England.

334
00:14:23,759 --> 00:14:26,910
那个业余传道士 多好的人啊
Oh, the lay preacher! What a nice chap!

335
00:14:30,079 --> 00:14:32,274
干嘛这么叫他?      他就是
Why do you call him that?       He is.

336
00:14:32,439 --> 00:14:34,873
是吗? 这是好事吧?
Is he? That's good, isn't it?

337
00:14:36,121 --> 00:14:38,509
好得不能再好了
Oh... good is exactly the word.

338
00:14:38,679 --> 00:14:42,470
他真是个大好人 还很出色地主持过
He's a really good man. Did a really good job

339
00:14:42,479 --> 00:14:44,470
白鳕鱼管理局的工作 不是吗?
at the White Fish Authority, too, didn't he?

340
00:14:44,639 --> 00:14:45,915
他在哪传道?
Where does he preach?

341
00:14:45,915 --> 00:14:47,915
不外乎教堂里吧
In church, I imagine.

342
00:14:48,079 --> 00:14:50,869
他这人虔诚得可怕 诚实得不像话
He's frightfully religious and terribly honest.

343
00:14:50,869 --> 00:14:52,869
对谁都绝对诚实
Honest with absolutely everybody.

344
00:14:53,039 --> 00:14:55,032
是吗? 那太好了
Is he? That is good.

345
00:14:55,039 --> 00:14:56,817
当然好 有百利而无一弊
Of course it's good. On the whole.

346
00:14:58,039 --> 00:15:00,030
只要他发现任何地方有丑闻
If he finds a scandal anywhere -

347
00:15:00,199 --> 00:15:02,556
哪怕是10号里的
even here in No.10 -

348
00:15:02,556 --> 00:15:04,556
也一定会昭告天下 绝无二话
he'll tell everybody, no doubt about that.

349
00:15:05,799 --> 00:15:07,563
你是说他不谨慎?
You mean he's indiscreet?

350
00:15:07,563 --> 00:15:09,792
天啊 这个词太贬义了
Oh, dear, that's such a pejorative word.

351
00:15:09,959 --> 00:15:13,556
我宁愿称此为择善固执
I'd prefer to say he's obsessively honest.

352
00:15:13,959 --> 00:15:15,556
好吧 你也觉得他能救金融城吧?
He's the right man to bring the City into line?

353
00:15:15,719 --> 00:15:18,313
还用说...如果您想要个圣人
Oh, absolu... If you want a saint.

354
00:15:19,759 --> 00:15:21,547
当然 也有些人说他
Of course, there are those who say

355
00:15:21,759 --> 00:15:23,547
跟现实世界脱节
he doesn't live in the real world.

356
00:15:23,719 --> 00:15:25,314
他这人极度道学
He is extremely puritanical,

357
00:15:25,319 --> 00:15:27,314
比一般圣经狂都严重
even for a Bible basher.

358
00:15:28,639 --> 00:15:29,631
真的?
Is he?

359
00:15:29,639 --> 00:15:31,631
是啊 都有点原教旨主义的味道了
Oh, yes. A bit of an ayatollah, in fact.

360
00:15:31,799 --> 00:15:33,997
您真打算找位力士参孙
Do you want to risk a Samson who might

361
00:15:33,999 --> 00:15:35,997
摧垮整座大厦 埋葬所有人吗?
bring the whole edifice crashing down?

362
00:15:36,159 --> 00:15:38,152
这倒得提防着点 是吗?
Yeah, that's a worry, isn't it?

363
00:15:38,159 --> 00:15:40,152
对 他对个人毫不尊重
He's no respecter of persons.

364
00:15:40,319 --> 00:15:42,058
尽管有时候冒犯别人
Although treading on toes is sometimes

365
00:15:42,058 --> 00:15:44,517
是迫不得已 他却养成习惯了
a necessity, he makes it a hobby.

366
00:15:44,679 --> 00:15:46,672
他喜欢什么事都开诚布公
He likes everything out in the open.

367
00:15:46,679 --> 00:15:48,672
他对媒体从不避讳
He talks very freely to the press.

368
00:15:48,839 --> 00:15:52,471
老实说 他这人不算...特别现实
In fact, he's not... awfully realistic.

369
00:15:52,839 --> 00:15:54,471
你还知道他别的情况吗?
Do you know anything else about him?

370
00:15:54,639 --> 00:15:59,633
当然 如此的完人难免让人起疑心
Well, one wonders if anybody can be that moral.

371
00:15:59,799 --> 00:16:03,269
我听说...      什么?
I've heard...      Yes?

372
00:16:05,359 --> 00:16:06,951
算了
No.

373
00:16:08,479 --> 00:16:11,551
算了 没事 肯定不会捅出来的
No, nothing. I'm sure it won't come out.

374
00:16:11,719 --> 00:16:13,516
什么?
What?

375
00:16:14,119 --> 00:16:16,110
没事 没事
No, nothing.

376
00:16:17,519 --> 00:16:19,510
我相信绝对没事
I'm sure it's nothing.

377
00:16:26,199 --> 00:16:28,157
财政部常任秘书到了 汉弗莱爵士
Permanent Secretary of the Treasury, sir.

378
00:16:28,199 --> 00:16:29,157
弗兰克 亲爱的朋友
My dear chap.

379
00:16:29,319 --> 00:16:31,310
汉弗莱      快坐
Humphrey.       Sit down.

380
00:16:31,479 --> 00:16:33,916
谢谢 我怎么听到传言说
Thanks. What's this rumour I hear

381
00:16:33,916 --> 00:16:35,916
你在抹黑詹森?
that you're rubbishing Jameson?

382
00:16:36,079 --> 00:16:39,472
那个业余传道士? 我觉得他不错啊
The lay preacher? I think he's a splendid chap.

383
00:16:39,472 --> 00:16:41,472
得了 别跟我来这招 汉弗莱
No. Don't play that game with me, Humphrey.

384
00:16:41,639 --> 00:16:44,456
财政部想让他当董事长
The Treasury wants him to be the new Governor.

385
00:16:45,092 --> 00:16:45,712
为什么?
Why?

386
00:16:46,439 --> 00:16:48,910
因为是时候给中央银行选位
It's time the Governor of the Bank of England

387
00:16:48,910 --> 00:16:50,910
聪明又有能力的董事长了
was intelligent and competent.

388
00:16:51,799 --> 00:16:53,630
这可是创举
It'd be an innovation.

389
00:16:54,799 --> 00:16:56,587
你不觉得值得一试吗?
Don't you think it should be tryed?

390
00:16:56,799 --> 00:16:58,587
可这太危险了
But it's so dangerous.

391
00:16:58,759 --> 00:17:01,956
汉弗莱 金融城的丑闻一桩接一桩
Look, we keep enduring these City scandals.

392
00:17:02,119 --> 00:17:04,422
财政部和部长都受够了
The Chancellor is fed up

393
00:17:04,422 --> 00:17:06,397
整天辩不可辩之理了
with having to defend the indefensible.

394
00:17:06,559 --> 00:17:09,027
对 弗兰克 我明白
Look, Frank, I understand.

395
00:17:09,199 --> 00:17:11,635
你得照顾财政部长的利益
You're looking after the Chancellor's interests.

396
00:17:11,635 --> 00:17:12,635
这是你的职责
That's your job.

397
00:17:12,799 --> 00:17:15,793
我得照顾首相的利益
I'm looking after the Prime Minister's interests

398
00:17:15,799 --> 00:17:17,793
还有国家利益 这是我的职责
and the nation's. That's mine.

399
00:17:17,959 --> 00:17:20,191
汉弗莱 一个诚实的财政部门
An honest financial sector

400
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:22,191
不可能对国家利益有害
can't damage the national interest.

401
00:17:22,359 --> 00:17:24,350
从长远来讲 可能有益
In the long term, it's a plus.

402
00:17:24,519 --> 00:17:26,513
不幸的是 从短期来讲你也知道
Unfortunately, in the short term, an inquiry

403
00:17:26,519 --> 00:17:29,513
对金融城发起调查会造成信用贬值
into the City would mean a loss of confidence.

404
00:17:29,679 --> 00:17:32,450
英镑会跳水 股价会跳水
The pound would plunge, shares would plunge

405
00:17:32,450 --> 00:17:34,070
政府也会跟着跳水
and the government would plunge.

406
00:17:34,239 --> 00:17:37,276
这个嘛 恐怕就是YP了
Ah, well, I'm afraid that's YP.

407
00:17:38,799 --> 00:17:40,118
YP?
YP?

408
00:17:40,999 --> 00:17:42,830
你的问题
Your problem.

409
00:17:49,239 --> 00:17:52,436
实际上 弗兰克 这我可说不准
Actually, Frank... I'm not so sure.

410
00:17:53,199 --> 00:17:55,989
你知道 大约六成
As you know, about 60%

411
00:17:55,989 --> 00:17:57,989
贝伦森银行的呆账坏账
of Phillips Berenson's outstanding loans

412
00:17:58,159 --> 00:18:00,878
都贷给了三家名声欠佳的外国客户
are with three foreigners of dubious repute.

413
00:18:01,039 --> 00:18:03,351
中央银行有责任
The Bank of England is responsible

414
00:18:03,351 --> 00:18:05,351
监督贝伦森银行
for supervising Phillips Berenson.

415
00:18:05,519 --> 00:18:06,592
可他们的监督漏洞百出
That's been a farce.

416
00:18:06,592 --> 00:18:09,592
我知道 调查员全是外行嘛
Their investigators are a bunch of amateurs.

417
00:18:09,759 --> 00:18:11,354
可谁又有责任监督
But who's responsible for supervising

418
00:18:11,759 --> 00:18:13,354
中央银行呢?
the Bank of England?

419
00:18:15,639 --> 00:18:19,234
财政部 不是吗?      没错...
The Treasury, isn't it?      Well, yes...

420
00:18:19,399 --> 00:18:21,995
我怎能告诉财政部长 如果我们清理整顿
How can I tell the Chancellor that if we have a clean-up

421
00:18:21,995 --> 00:18:23,995
责任可能变成他的?
he may be held responsible?

422
00:18:24,159 --> 00:18:26,995
那他就真要辩不可辩之理了
He'd be defending the really indefensible then.

423
00:18:26,995 --> 00:18:29,995
他会需要首相很多支持的
He'd need an awful lot of support from the PM.

424
00:18:30,159 --> 00:18:32,115
对 可他应该能得到吧
Yes, but he'd get it, presumably.

425
00:18:32,279 --> 00:18:34,279
首相也不喜欢辩不可辩之理
The PM isn't keen on defending the indefensible.

426
00:18:34,279 --> 00:18:37,069
会很难说服他的
He'd need a lot of convincing.

427
00:18:37,239 --> 00:18:41,348
财政部长得说 他是受了
The Chancellor would have to tell him that he'd

428
00:18:41,348 --> 00:18:43,348
财政部官员的误导 弗兰克
been let down by his Treasury officials, Frank.

429
00:18:44,199 --> 00:18:46,190
可是...可是...可是...
But... But... But...

430
00:18:48,119 --> 00:18:49,837
你的问题?
YP?

431
00:18:55,639 --> 00:18:58,358
你说得太对了 这真可怕
You're absolutely right, this is frightful.

432
00:18:59,279 --> 00:19:02,050
疏忽大意和玩忽职守之间的
What's the difference between irregularities

433
00:19:02,050 --> 00:19:02,874
分界线究竟在哪?
and malpractices?

434
00:19:04,079 --> 00:19:06,392
证据不足的罪过叫做疏忽大意
Irregularity means it's a crime you can't prove.

435
00:19:06,392 --> 00:19:09,392
证据确凿的罪过就叫玩忽职守
Malpractice means it's a crime you can prove.

436
00:19:10,399 --> 00:19:11,435
还有人看过这个吗?
Anyone else seen this?

437
00:19:11,435 --> 00:19:12,435
没有了
Nobody.

438
00:19:12,599 --> 00:19:15,321
我们怎么会拿到贝伦森银行的
How did we get this secret auditor's report

439
00:19:15,321 --> 00:19:16,069
秘密审计报告?
on Phillips Berenson?

440
00:19:16,239 --> 00:19:19,546
会计师事务所的合伙人跟我有交情
A partner at the accountant's is a friend.

441
00:19:19,546 --> 00:19:20,027
只为了交情?
Just friendship?

442
00:19:20,199 --> 00:19:22,249
他似乎很期待看到
He's looking forward to reading

443
00:19:22,249 --> 00:19:23,794
明年的授勋名单
the New Year's Honours List.

444
00:19:24,799 --> 00:19:28,075
好吧 我们怎么办? 找哪个部门?
All right. How do we do it? Which section?

445
00:19:28,239 --> 00:19:30,073
何不通过威尔士事务部
What about through the Welsh Office

446
00:19:30,239 --> 00:19:32,073
表彰他泄露消息有功?
for services to LEEKS!

447
00:19:35,239 --> 00:19:38,322
我真惊讶巴特莱银行居然
It surprises me that Bartlett's Bank should be

448
00:19:38,322 --> 00:19:40,724
卷入这么深 你不惊讶吗?
so deeply involved. Doesn't it surprise you?

449
00:19:40,724 --> 00:19:43,353
有格雷布克做主席 不稀奇
Not with Sir Desmond Glazebrook as chairman.

450
00:19:43,353 --> 00:19:45,353
他到底怎么当上主席的?
How on earth did he become chairman?

451
00:19:45,519 --> 00:19:47,742
他从没什么新点子
He never has any original ideas,

452
00:19:47,742 --> 00:19:49,228
从来不坚持原则
never takes a stand on principle.

453
00:19:49,399 --> 00:19:53,110
而且他什么都不懂 会附和任何人
As he doesn't understand anything, he agrees with everybody

454
00:19:53,399 --> 00:19:55,470
所以人们都觉得他可靠
and so people think he's sound.

455
00:19:55,470 --> 00:19:57,113
因为这些我才请他来参谋
Is that why I've been invited to consult him

456
00:19:57,279 --> 00:19:59,113
董事长的人选吗?
about this governorship?

457
00:19:59,279 --> 00:20:01,270
他几分钟内就到
He's due in a few minutes.

458
00:20:01,439 --> 00:20:03,531
您大概会发现 他不愿意您
You may find he doesn't want you

459
00:20:03,531 --> 00:20:05,876
任命詹森来做清理整顿
to appoint Jameson to do a clean-up.

460
00:20:06,039 --> 00:20:09,001
有了这个 没选择了
No option after this.

461
00:20:08,599 --> 00:20:10,159
肯定得走漏些风声
Some of it's bound to.

462
00:20:10,159 --> 00:20:11,159
如果上法庭的话
If it gets to court.

463
00:20:11,319 --> 00:20:13,193
由中央银行来援助
A Bank of England rescue

464
00:20:13,193 --> 00:20:14,629
能瞒住最坏的部分
will keep the worst of it quiet.

465
00:20:16,548 --> 00:20:18,712
格雷布克想要我任命谁?
Who will Glazebrook want me to appoint?

466
00:20:18,879 --> 00:20:20,508
戴斯蒙-格雷布克 首相
Desmond Glazebrook.

467
00:20:20,879 --> 00:20:22,508
太对了 伯纳
Absolutely right, Bernard.

468
00:20:25,319 --> 00:20:27,310
关于什么?      你开玩笑吧?
What about?      You're not serious?

469
00:20:27,479 --> 00:20:30,313
掩盖起来的话 谁得利最大?
Who has the most interest in a cover-up?

470
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:31,313
格雷布克他自己
Sir Desmond Glazebrook.

471
00:20:31,479 --> 00:20:32,985
请他进来
Ask him in.

472
00:20:32,985 --> 00:20:34,391
汉弗莱爵士和他在一起 都请进来
Sir Humphrey's with him. Send them in.

473
00:20:34,559 --> 00:20:36,871
他们都知道这些了吧?
They'll know about this?

474
00:20:36,871 --> 00:20:38,871
对 可他们不必知道您知道
Yes, but they mustn't know that you know.

475
00:20:39,039 --> 00:20:41,507
不然得给那合伙人伯爵头衔了
Or you'll have to make the partner an earl.

476
00:20:42,879 --> 00:20:46,302
戴斯蒙爵士 多谢你大驾光临
Ah, Sir Desmond, how good of you to come.

477
00:20:46,302 --> 00:20:46,667
首相
Prime Minister.

478
00:20:46,839 --> 00:20:49,433
快请坐
Do sit down, won't you?

479
00:20:50,955 --> 00:20:54,581
你们知道 我得任命一位
Now, as you know... I've got to appoint

480
00:20:54,581 --> 00:20:56,311
新的中央银行董事长
a new Governor for the Bank of England.

481
00:20:56,479 --> 00:20:57,870
我想听听你的看法
I'd welcome your views.

482
00:20:57,879 --> 00:21:00,870
对 我也觉得该任命一位
Well, I certainly think you should appoint one.

483
00:21:02,159 --> 00:21:04,198
我觉得首相已经差不多
I think the Prime Minister's

484
00:21:04,198 --> 00:21:06,198
决定要这么做了
more or less decided that.

485
00:21:06,359 --> 00:21:07,351
问题是任命谁
The question is whom.

486
00:21:07,359 --> 00:21:09,351
啊 这可难说了
Ah, that's tricky.

487
00:21:09,519 --> 00:21:11,828
得找个大伙信得过的
Needs to be someone the chaps trust.

488
00:21:11,999 --> 00:21:14,878
我觉得我们要找的人得聪明
I feel we need someone who's intelligent,

489
00:21:14,999 --> 00:21:15,878
有活力 正直
energetic, upright.

490
00:21:16,039 --> 00:21:19,509
呃 等等      你不同意?
Er, well, hold on.      You don't agree?

491
00:21:19,679 --> 00:21:22,275
当然 这主意挺有意思的
Well, of course, it's a jolly interesting idea,

492
00:21:22,679 --> 00:21:24,275
首相
Prime Minister.

493
00:21:24,439 --> 00:21:27,237
可大伙不一定信得过这种家伙
Not sure the chaps would trust that sort of chap.

494
00:21:27,399 --> 00:21:30,315
首相正担心金融丑闻的事
The PM is worried about financial scandals.

495
00:21:30,399 --> 00:21:33,315
你担心金融丑闻吗 戴斯蒙爵士?
Are you worried about financial scandals?

496
00:21:33,479 --> 00:21:36,076
当然 这种事没有最好 可是...
Of course, we don't want any of those, but...

497
00:21:36,079 --> 00:21:39,076
要是你选的是大伙信任的家伙
if you go for the sort of chap the chaps trust,

498
00:21:39,239 --> 00:21:41,739
你自己也不信他这种家伙
you can trust him to be the sort of chap to see

499
00:21:41,739 --> 00:21:44,871
会不让大伙卷进什么丑闻
the chaps don't get involved in any scandals.

500
00:21:45,039 --> 00:21:47,428
他只会掩盖起来      不 一有什么可疑
He'd hush them up.      No, any suspicion,

501
00:21:47,599 --> 00:21:50,591
你马上请那家伙吃个便饭
and you have the chap straight out for lunch.

502
00:21:52,319 --> 00:21:54,709
问问他有没有这回事
Ask him if there's anything in it.

503
00:21:54,719 --> 00:21:55,709
要是他说没有呢?
What if he says no?

504
00:21:56,599 --> 00:21:58,069
信得过的家伙说话 你得信嘛
You have to trust a chap's word.

505
00:21:58,599 --> 00:22:00,069
金融城就是这样
That's how the City works.

506
00:22:00,239 --> 00:22:02,976
你对贝伦森银行了解多少?
What do you know about Phillips Berenson?

507
00:22:03,712 --> 00:22:06,030
你对贝伦森银行了解多少?
What do YOU know about Phillips Berenson?

508
00:22:06,199 --> 00:22:09,271
这个...就是报上披露那些
Well, er, only what I read in the papers.

509
00:22:09,439 --> 00:22:11,157
那就好
Oh, good.

510
00:22:12,199 --> 00:22:15,034
是啊 他们有点麻烦 借了笔小钱给
Yes, well, they lent a bit of money

511
00:22:15,199 --> 00:22:17,034
不该借的人 人非圣贤啊
to the wrong chaps. Could happen to anyone.

512
00:22:17,199 --> 00:22:19,056
你没听到任何传言?
You haven't heard rumours?

513
00:22:19,056 --> 00:22:20,111
传言随时都有
There are always rumours.

514
00:22:20,279 --> 00:22:22,795
关于贿赂? 侵吞?
Of bribery? Embezzlement?

515
00:22:22,795 --> 00:22:24,795
挪用资金? 内线交易?
Misappropriation? Insider dealing?

516
00:22:24,959 --> 00:22:27,553
亲爱的女士 话说重了吧
Dear lady, those are strong words.

517
00:22:27,553 --> 00:22:28,395
你是说都不存在?
So they're not true?

518
00:22:28,999 --> 00:22:31,613
这个嘛...可以用不同...
Well, er, there are different... er...

519
00:22:31,613 --> 00:22:33,356
不同角度来看同一件事
different ways of looking at things.

520
00:22:34,359 --> 00:22:35,632
要用什么奇异角度
What's a different way

521
00:22:35,632 --> 00:22:37,954
来看非法侵吞?
of looking at embezzlement?

522
00:22:38,119 --> 00:22:40,872
要是谁侵吞 你得采取点措施
If a chap embezzles, you have to do something.

523
00:22:41,039 --> 00:22:42,494
严厉警告他一下?
Have a serious word with him?

524
00:22:42,494 --> 00:22:43,998
那当然
Absolutely.

525
00:22:44,599 --> 00:22:46,194
不过通常那家伙只是
Usually it's just a chap

526
00:22:46,599 --> 00:22:48,194
自作主张支了一笔短期的
who's advanced himself a short-term,

527
00:22:48,359 --> 00:22:50,352
非正式 无担保的临时贷款
unauthorised, unsecured temporary loan

528
00:22:50,359 --> 00:22:52,352
朝公司借了点钱
from the company's account

529
00:22:52,519 --> 00:22:54,555
不幸投错了地方
and invested it unluckily.

530
00:22:56,279 --> 00:22:59,430
人有失手 马有失蹄嘛
Horse falls at the first fence, that sort of thing.

531
00:22:59,599 --> 00:23:02,912
那你觉得我该任命谁?
So who do you think I should appoint?

532
00:23:02,912 --> 00:23:04,912
就像我说的 这不好办
Oh, well, as I say, that's not easy.

533
00:23:05,079 --> 00:23:08,230
找不出几个大伙都信得过的人
Not all that many chaps the chaps trust.

534
00:23:08,399 --> 00:23:09,960
这不由我来说
It's not for me to say,

535
00:23:09,960 --> 00:23:11,492
不过如果受到了邀请...
but if one were to be asked...

536
00:23:11,492 --> 00:23:14,871
既然这个人被认为是...
As long as one were thought to be...

537
00:23:14,871 --> 00:23:16,871
当然 人各有志 可是...
Of course, one is committed, but...

538
00:23:17,039 --> 00:23:18,912
如果真是形势所迫...
And if one were to be pressed,

539
00:23:18,912 --> 00:23:21,635
我敢说这个人总能腾出时间来
I dare say one could make oneself available.

540
00:23:22,999 --> 00:23:25,274
就当作是为...
As a duty one owes to...

541
00:23:25,439 --> 00:23:28,636
我想的是亚历山大-詹森
I was thinking of Alexander Jameson.

542
00:23:28,799 --> 00:23:30,109
你觉得呢?
What's your view?

543
00:23:30,799 --> 00:23:32,109
他是个好会计
Well, he's a good accountant.

544
00:23:32,279 --> 00:23:33,871
诚实吗?      对
Honest?      Yes.

545
00:23:34,039 --> 00:23:36,428
精力呢?      恐怕也不错
Energetic?      I'm afraid so.

546
00:23:36,599 --> 00:23:38,988
可你会推荐他吗?      不会
But would you recommend him?      No.

547
00:23:39,159 --> 00:23:41,471
为什么不会?
Why not?

548
00:23:41,471 --> 00:23:43,471
金融城的事很难说的 首相
Well, the City's a funny place, Prime Minister.

549
00:23:43,639 --> 00:23:45,348
一旦你露了馅
If you spill the beans,

550
00:23:45,639 --> 00:23:47,348
开弓可没有回头箭
you open up a whole can of worms.

551
00:23:48,239 --> 00:23:50,232
要是您不想招来苍蝇
How can you let sleeping dogs lie

552
00:23:50,239 --> 00:23:52,232
又怎能去捅马蜂窝?
if you let the cat out of the bag?

553
00:23:54,799 --> 00:23:56,998
要想注入新血 一不小心
Bring in a new broom and, if you're not careful,

554
00:23:56,998 --> 00:23:59,998
可能就得刮骨疗毒顺带割肉
you've thrown the baby out with the bath water.

555
00:24:01,559 --> 00:24:05,757
临阵突然换了将
If you change horses in the middle of the stream,

556
00:24:05,919 --> 00:24:08,956
四面楚歌也怨不得谁
then you're up the creek without a paddle.

557
00:24:09,119 --> 00:24:11,952
于是就吹灯拔蜡了
And then the balloon goes up!

558
00:24:12,599 --> 00:24:14,988
可不是 被他们抓住小辫子了嘛
Obviously. They hit you for six.

559
00:24:16,679 --> 00:24:18,476
等于自摆乌龙
An own goal, in fact.

560
00:24:23,359 --> 00:24:24,611
我还有半小时就要上台了
I'm on in half an hour

561
00:24:24,611 --> 00:24:26,271
讲话里还是没有任何实质内容
and this speech is devoid of content.

562
00:24:26,439 --> 00:24:27,636
我不知道
Oh, I don't know.

563
00:24:27,639 --> 00:24:29,636
你觉得呢 伯纳?
What do you think, Bernard?

564
00:24:29,799 --> 00:24:32,518
我不知道      好吧 我知道
I don't know.      Well, I do know.

565
00:24:32,679 --> 00:24:34,638
观众会起立鼓掌的
It'll get a standing ovation.

566
00:24:36,083 --> 00:24:36,638
鼓多久?
Oh. How long?

567
00:24:36,799 --> 00:24:38,790
三分半钟
Three and a half minutes.

568
00:24:38,959 --> 00:24:40,110
他们都有秒表不成?
Have people got stopwatches

569
00:24:40,110 --> 00:24:42,110
今天就发
Issued them today.

570
00:24:43,119 --> 00:24:45,328
首相 汉弗莱爵士陪同布兰达高级专员
Sir Humphrey's downstairs with the Burandan

571
00:24:45,328 --> 00:24:47,715
在楼下等候 能见见他们吗?
High Commissioner. Could they have a word?

572
00:24:47,879 --> 00:24:50,473
布兰达高级...      他说十万火急
Burandan High...?      He says it's urgent.

573
00:24:50,639 --> 00:24:54,268
怎么...好吧 他最好快点
Oh, all right. He'd better be quick.

574
00:24:54,439 --> 00:24:56,035
不能讲鼓励投资吗?
Can't we talk about getting more investment?

575
00:24:56,439 --> 00:24:59,035
没法鼓励 利息率太高了
Interest rates are too high.

576
00:24:59,199 --> 00:25:01,785
您不能胁迫财政部长胁迫财政部
Can't you lean on the Chancellor to lean on

577
00:25:01,785 --> 00:25:03,989
胁迫中央银行胁迫各银行降息吗?
the Bank of England to lean on the banks?

578
00:25:04,159 --> 00:25:07,754
半小时之内? 一年半载都难
What, in half an hour? Not in a month of Sundays!

579
00:25:07,919 --> 00:25:09,569
中央银行绝对不同意
The Bank would never allow it.

580
00:25:09,569 --> 00:25:12,709
我能做的 只有任命清廉先生当董事长了
All I can do is appoint Mr Clean as Governor.

581
00:25:12,879 --> 00:25:14,817
"哈克拒绝继续姑息"
"Hacker will take no more nonsense

582
00:25:14,817 --> 00:25:16,088
"金融城的丑闻"
from the City."

583
00:25:16,439 --> 00:25:17,388
首相
Prime Minister.

584
00:25:17,439 --> 00:25:21,388
专员先生 真是意外之喜啊
High Commissioner, an unexpected pleasure!

585
00:25:21,559 --> 00:25:24,027
快请进 请坐下
Do come in. Sit down, please.

586
00:25:25,565 --> 00:25:26,394
有什么可以效劳的?
Now, what can I do for you?

587
00:25:26,559 --> 00:25:28,347
首相 高级专员先生
Well, the High Commissioner's

588
00:25:28,559 --> 00:25:30,347
担心的是传闻中
concerned about the rumour

589
00:25:30,519 --> 00:25:32,509
您要任命詹森
that you intend to appoint Jameson

590
00:25:32,519 --> 00:25:33,909
管理中央银行的事
to the Bank of England,

591
00:25:34,079 --> 00:25:36,945
因为他必然会深入调查
which will inevitably create an investigation

592
00:25:36,945 --> 00:25:38,713
贝伦森银行一案
into Phillips Berenson.

593
00:25:38,799 --> 00:25:41,791
抱歉 不过这和布兰达有何关系?
Forgive me, but how does this concern Buranda?

594
00:25:41,959 --> 00:25:43,668
贝伦森这家问题银行
Phillips Berenson is a shady bank

595
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:45,668
把自己60%的资本贷给了
that lent 60% of its money

596
00:25:45,839 --> 00:25:48,399
三家名声欠佳的外国客户
to three foreigners of doubtful repute.

597
00:25:48,559 --> 00:25:50,552
这三家客户之中两家
Two of those three foreigners

598
00:25:50,559 --> 00:25:52,552
分别是布兰达总统
were the President of Buranda

599
00:25:52,719 --> 00:25:56,507
和布兰达企业集团主席
and the Chairman of the Burandan Corporation.

600
00:25:57,559 --> 00:25:59,448
如果您威胁到这些贷款
If you attack these loans,

601
00:25:59,448 --> 00:26:01,552
布兰达总统就不得不
the President of Buranda will have no option

602
00:26:01,719 --> 00:26:03,189
将此视为
but to interpret this move

603
00:26:03,719 --> 00:26:05,843
敌对和种族主义行径
as a hostile and racist act.

604
00:26:05,843 --> 00:26:07,315
种族主义?      当然
Racist?      Of course.

605
00:26:07,479 --> 00:26:10,458
我无意冒犯贵国总统本身
I've no intention of attacking the President

606
00:26:10,458 --> 00:26:11,995
我只打算...
per se. L-I would merely...

607
00:26:12,159 --> 00:26:14,761
说他名声欠佳
Say that he was someone of dubious repute.

608
00:26:14,761 --> 00:26:17,187
对...不不不
Yes. No, no, no.

609
00:26:17,359 --> 00:26:18,997
我...我...
I... I...

610
00:26:19,159 --> 00:26:21,764
请允许我进一步指出 以种族主义
May I further point out that a racist attack

611
00:26:21,764 --> 00:26:22,754
攻击我国总统
on our President

612
00:26:22,919 --> 00:26:26,922
毫无疑问会令非洲所有其它国家
would undoubtedly create solidarity and support

613
00:26:26,922 --> 00:26:28,742
同仇敌忾起来
from all the other African states.

614
00:26:28,742 --> 00:26:30,523
英联邦国家 首相
Commonwealth countries.

615
00:26:30,523 --> 00:26:31,973
我们会齐心协力 将英国
We would move to have Britain

616
00:26:31,973 --> 00:26:33,917
驱逐出英联邦
expelled from the Commonwealth.

617
00:26:34,839 --> 00:26:37,208
总统首当其冲就得取消
The President would be obliged to cancel

618
00:26:37,208 --> 00:26:39,230
女王陛下下月的国事访问
Her Majesty's state visit next month

619
00:26:39,399 --> 00:26:42,735
布兰达将立刻抛售所有
and Buranda would sell all the British

620
00:26:42,735 --> 00:26:44,528
它购买的英国国债
government stock that it has bought.

621
00:26:44,528 --> 00:26:46,229
英镑会贬值吧?
Would that create a run on the pound?

622
00:26:46,759 --> 00:26:47,229
是啊
Yes.

623
00:26:47,399 --> 00:26:50,391
还有吗?      还不够吗?
Anything else?      Isn't that enough?

624
00:26:50,559 --> 00:26:52,801
专员先生 能否允许我
High Commissioner, will you excuse me

625
00:26:52,801 --> 00:26:55,758
和汉弗莱爵士私下说几句话?
if I have a few words with Sir Humphrey?

626
00:26:55,919 --> 00:26:58,754
太感谢了 多谢您大驾光临
Thank you so much. So good of you to come

627
00:26:58,919 --> 00:27:00,754
不远万里来到我国
and... such a long way.

628
00:27:00,919 --> 00:27:02,707
我会积极考虑您的话的
I'll give your words earnest consideration.

629
00:27:02,919 --> 00:27:04,707
那就好
Please do.

630
00:27:08,319 --> 00:27:11,347
汉弗莱 你竟敢害我落进这步田地
How dare you put me in this position!

631
00:27:11,347 --> 00:27:13,347
不是我 首相 是布兰达
It is not I, but Buranda.

632
00:27:13,519 --> 00:27:15,898
考虑到英联邦传统 您更应该
The Commonwealth club is another reason

633
00:27:15,898 --> 00:27:17,228
三思而后行
you should exercise caution.

634
00:27:17,399 --> 00:27:19,390
布兰达总统是个骗子
The President is a crook!

635
00:27:19,559 --> 00:27:22,298
怎能让他混进英联邦来
He shouldn't be a member of the club.

636
00:27:22,298 --> 00:27:23,108
应该把他赶出去
He should be blackballed.

637
00:27:23,279 --> 00:27:24,370
他们已经出去了
He is already.

638
00:27:24,370 --> 00:27:26,271
对 谢谢 伯纳
Yes, thank you, Bernard.

639
00:27:27,839 --> 00:27:30,832
我真想不通 汉弗莱
I don't understand it, Humphrey.

640
00:27:30,839 --> 00:27:31,832
你玩的什么花招?
What's your game?

641
00:27:31,999 --> 00:27:33,813
你凭什么觉得
Why should I

642
00:27:33,813 --> 00:27:35,164
我会掩盖又一桩丑闻?
allow another cover-up?

643
00:27:35,164 --> 00:27:35,992
你能得什么好处?
What's in it for you?

644
00:27:36,159 --> 00:27:38,264
什么也没有 首相 我向您保证
Nothing, Prime Minister! I assure you,

645
00:27:38,264 --> 00:27:40,755
我毫无任何私人动机
I have no private ulterior motive.

646
00:27:40,919 --> 00:27:43,521
我是在保护您免于自取灭亡
I'm trying to protect you from yourself.

647
00:27:43,521 --> 00:27:45,674
我完全站在您这边
I'm entirely on your side.

648
00:27:45,839 --> 00:27:46,735
我们凭什么相信?
How can we believe that?

649
00:27:46,735 --> 00:27:50,196
因为这次是真的
Because this time it's true!

650
00:27:52,439 --> 00:27:57,160
我是说 这次我尤其站在您这边
I mean, this time I am particularly on your side.

651
00:27:57,160 --> 00:27:58,673
我一定得找些好消息
I've got to say something good

652
00:27:58,839 --> 00:28:00,673
加进今天的讲话里
in my speech today.

653
00:28:00,839 --> 00:28:03,371
要是我不能宣布任命清廉先生
If I can't announce the appointment of Mr Clean

654
00:28:03,371 --> 00:28:04,309
当中央银行董事长...
as Governor...

655
00:28:04,479 --> 00:28:06,109
何不宣布银行降息呢?
Why not announce a cut in interest rates?

656
00:28:06,258 --> 00:28:09,109
别傻了 汉弗莱 我...什么?
Oh, don't be silly, I... What?

657
00:28:09,279 --> 00:28:11,429
何不宣布银行降息
Announce a cut in interest rates

658
00:28:11,599 --> 00:28:13,799
银行不会容忍政治降息的
The Bank couldn't allow a political cut -

659
00:28:13,799 --> 00:28:15,746
尤其是詹森董事长
particularly with Jameson.

660
00:28:15,746 --> 00:28:18,114
格雷布克董事长就可以
It would with Desmond Glazebrook.

661
00:28:18,114 --> 00:28:20,154
如果您任命他为董事长
Now, if you appoint him Governor,

662
00:28:20,319 --> 00:28:23,871
他明早就降低巴特莱银行的利率
he'll cut Bartlett's interest rates in the morning -

663
00:28:23,879 --> 00:28:26,239
您可以一起在讲话里宣布
you can announce both in your speech.

664
00:28:26,239 --> 00:28:27,270
你怎么知道?
How do you know?

665
00:28:27,270 --> 00:28:30,167
他刚告诉我的 他就在这里
He's just told me. He's here.

666
00:28:31,479 --> 00:28:33,472
戴斯蒙格雷布克当董事长?
Desmond Glazebrook as Governor?

667
00:28:33,479 --> 00:28:35,472
可他太蠢了
But he's such a fool.

668
00:28:35,639 --> 00:28:39,338
他满口都是陈词滥调 说起废话
He only talks in cliche. He can talk

669
00:28:39,338 --> 00:28:40,849
能说到海枯石烂
in cliche till the cows come home.

670
00:28:41,799 --> 00:28:43,745
要是降低利率
Won't a cut in interest rates

671
00:28:43,745 --> 00:28:45,506
物价不是会涨吗?
mean that prices will go up?

672
00:28:45,506 --> 00:28:46,440
我不在乎
I don't mind that,

673
00:28:46,440 --> 00:28:49,556
只要我得到通货膨胀...起立鼓掌
as long as I get a standing inflation... ovation.

674
00:28:49,719 --> 00:28:51,785
你不想金融城有个诚实的人?
You don't want an honest man in the City?

675
00:28:51,785 --> 00:28:55,157
格雷布克也不算...不诚实吧?
Glazebrook isn't exactly... dishonest, is he?

676
00:28:55,319 --> 00:28:57,132
不 他太蠢了 搞不清楚
No, he's too stupid to know

677
00:28:57,132 --> 00:28:58,789
自己到底诚不诚实
whether he's honest or not.

678
00:28:58,959 --> 00:29:02,497
政府总不能和金融城搞僵吧?
We can't operate without the City's goodwill,

679
00:29:02,497 --> 00:29:03,550
不能 首相
No, Prime Minister.

680
00:29:03,559 --> 00:29:07,184
也不该无谓地让他们难堪吧?
No point in embarrassing them needlessly.

681
00:29:07,184 --> 00:29:08,949
不该 首相
No, Prime Minister.

682
00:29:09,519 --> 00:29:11,835
多萝西 给我的讲稿加上
Dorothy, fix my speech to include

683
00:29:11,835 --> 00:29:13,846
降息的内容 好吗?
a cut in interest rates.

684
00:29:13,999 --> 00:29:16,957
汉弗莱 请戴斯蒙爵士过来
Humphrey, ask Sir Desmond to come up here.

685
00:29:17,119 --> 00:29:19,314
是 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

686
00:29:21,258 --> 00:29:31,570
